From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: xcbc, cmac, ccm - allow instantiation by a REQ_VIRT lookup

The core gives every async ahash without CRYPTO_ALG_REQ_VIRT a
fallback, and crypto_ahash_init_tfm() looks the fallback up with type
CRYPTO_ALG_REQ_VIRT. When no instance of the algorithm exists yet, the
lookup instantiates its template with that type. The xcbc, cmac and
cbcmac templates check the requested type against
CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SHASH alone, so crypto_check_attr_type() rejects the
REQ_VIRT bit and the instantiation fails with -EINVAL. The driver's
tfm then cannot be allocated, unless something created the software
instance earlier. For example, the self-test of the Broadcom SPU's
xcbc(aes) fails:

  alg: hash: failed to allocate transform for xcbc-aes-iproc: -22

Creating xcbc(aes-generic) first, through AF_ALG, makes the same
self-test pass.

Every shash is registered with CRYPTO_ALG_REQ_VIRT, so check the
requested type against CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SHASH | CRYPTO_ALG_REQ_VIRT.

Fixes: 9d7a0ab1c753 ("crypto: ahash - Handle partial blocks in API")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 crypto/ccm.c  | 3 ++-
 crypto/cmac.c | 3 ++-
 crypto/xcbc.c | 3 ++-
 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/crypto/ccm.c
+++ b/crypto/ccm.c
@@ -852,7 +852,8 @@ static int cbcmac_create(struct crypto_template *tmpl, struct rtattr **tb)
 	u32 mask;
 	int err;
 
-	err = crypto_check_attr_type(tb, CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SHASH, &mask);
+	err = crypto_check_attr_type(tb, CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SHASH |
+				     CRYPTO_ALG_REQ_VIRT, &mask);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
--- a/crypto/cmac.c
+++ b/crypto/cmac.c
@@ -180,7 +180,8 @@ static int cmac_create(struct crypto_template *tmpl, struct rtattr **tb)
 	u32 mask;
 	int err;
 
-	err = crypto_check_attr_type(tb, CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SHASH, &mask);
+	err = crypto_check_attr_type(tb, CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SHASH |
+				     CRYPTO_ALG_REQ_VIRT, &mask);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
--- a/crypto/xcbc.c
+++ b/crypto/xcbc.c
@@ -132,7 +132,8 @@ static int xcbc_create(struct crypto_template *tmpl, struct rtattr **tb)
 	u32 mask;
 	int err;
 
-	err = crypto_check_attr_type(tb, CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SHASH, &mask);
+	err = crypto_check_attr_type(tb, CRYPTO_ALG_TYPE_SHASH |
+				     CRYPTO_ALG_REQ_VIRT, &mask);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
